   "sources": [
    "https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/article/anthropic-publicly-files-ipo-prospectus-noting-strong-revenue-growth-and-massive-spending-131807138.html",
    "https://www.analyticsinsight.net/stocks/us-stock-market-wall-street-rebounds-as-anthropic-ipo-filing-lifts-tech-shares-ahead-of-fed-decision",
    "https://aiweekly.co/alerts/anthropic-s-1-shows-163b-h1-revenue-25-from-two-customers-and-807b-non-cash"
   ],
   "paragraph": "An S-1 is a disclosure document a company hands the US securities regulator before selling shares to the public, and on Monday Anthropic filed one, planning to list on Nasdaq as ANT. The headline numbers are lopsided: $16.3 billion of revenue in six months, against $4.6 billion in all of 2025. The net loss of $80.7 billion sounds like cash burned, but Yahoo Finance says most of it came from accounting charges, which are bookkeeping entries rather than money spent. The offer size and price range are unset and the date is unconfirmed. About a fifth of revenue came from two customers, though one outlet says 25%, so that share is disputed.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "tesla-spacex",
